# chatPlayerLose(Player player)
# Fires when the human checkmates the engine — the "ok I'm actually
# an AI" reveal. Triggered from interactEntity at the first
# checkGameOver call, gated on isCheckmate AND sideToMove ==
# playerColor (which together identify a checkmate against the
# engine, not against the human).
#
# Each @delay between lines is a "typing pause" so the messages
# trickle in the way a real player's chat would. The leading 80-tick
# delay lets the checkmate beat land first (player sees the move,
# then the bot starts revealing itself a few seconds later).
#
# Body is a TEST PLACEHOLDER — replace with the real reveal
# wording / pick from a flavor pool. Keep the (player) signature so
# the trigger stays unchanged.

@using rychess
@fast

@bypass /title @s times 0 100 20
@bypass playsound minecraft:entity.wither.spawn master @s ~ ~ ~ 1 1
@bypass title @s subtitle {"color":"#EC4642","text":"Press \"New Game\" to retry"}
@bypass title @s title {"bold":true,"color":"#E33E39","text":"Checkmate"}
